From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:45:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: pool large command BOs by size class

The Witcher 3 trace creates 74 command heaps/s because every upload above 128 KiB is destroyed at command-buffer reset. Retain idle large BOs in seven power-of-two classes, 256 KiB through 16 MiB, with a 64 MiB actual-byte cap per pool and oldest-returned-first eviction. Keep their residency membership until eviction, trim or destruction. Requests above the largest class bypass the cache. On device-memory allocation failure, empty idle large BOs and retry once.

Reset/free/implicit Begin return resources only after the recording is no longer needed. Release-resources pool reset and trim empty the idle cache. Initialize/reset the existing small-BO free count and enforce its exact 32-BO cap. Count pooled command bytes separately in the memory census and report cumulative new/reused large BOs.

Linear: PLA-464
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-10-28-kk-large-command-bo-pool.md
Offered-upstream: no
